// The editor side of the database: an object manipulator (IObjMan) reading and
// writing fields by path, inserting into and removing from arrays, iterating
// fields, and a new object saved to disk.
//
// Nival's TestDB covered this, as an executable that ran each check once and
// then returned 0 whatever they found. The checks and their data are carried
// over: the schema is TestDB/TestType.cll, generated by dbcodegen into the TestDB
// library, and the records are TestDB/data. The database runs on a copy of
// them, since opening it writes an index and the last test writes a new object.
//
// Every field is checked through the three routes the editor relies on to agree:
// set and get by path, set by path and read the C++ struct, and write the struct
// and get by path. Fields marked noCode have no struct member; the database
// keeps their values itself, and they are checked by path only.

